==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{af|es|en-|pieza|-ar}}, possibly through a {{inh|es|VL.|-}} root {{m|la|*impettiāre}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr|+<audio:LL-Q1321 (spa)-AdrianAbdulBaha-empezar.wav<a:Colombia>>}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|<ie>}}

# to [[start]], [[begin]], to [[get started]]
#: {{syn|es|comenzar|iniciar}}
# {{indtr|es|a}} to start to
#: {{ux|es|Hace poco que '''empezó''' a comer vegetales.|He recently '''started''' eating vegetables.}}
# {{indtr|es|por}} to start by; to start with
#: {{ux|es|Sugiero que '''empecemos''' por reconocer que necesitamos más ayuda.|I suggest that '''we start''' by acknowledging that we need more help.}}
#: {{ux|es|En español, pocas palabras '''empiezan''' por la letra ñ.|In Spanish, few words '''begin''' with the letter ñ.}}
# {{indtr|es|con}} to [[lead]] [[with]], to [[open]] [[with]]
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to be [[started]]

